course: dictionary
lesson: 7179
title: One word, many meanings: person
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word person can mean one human being, but it has other meanings too. Read the words around it to find out which one is used. «A seat is for a person, so put your bag on your lap or the floor when the bus is busy.» Here a person is one human, so one seat is for one human.
explain: Look for clue words. «Meet in person» means meeting face to face, really there, not on the phone or on a screen. The words in person tell you which meaning to pick.
explain: In grammar, person tells you who is speaking. I is first person, you is second person, and he or she is third person. Here person is a grammar word, not a word for a human.
fact: A person is a man, woman or child, one human being.
fact: The plural of person is people, though persons is also used.
fact: «In person» means really there, not on the phone or on a screen.
fact: «Per person» means for each person, as in a price or a share.
fact: In grammar, first person is I, second person is you, and third person is he or she.
exercise: «A seat is for a person, so put your bag on your lap or the floor when the bus is busy.» What does person mean here? | Really there, not on a screen | A share of a price | *One human being | A grammar word for who is speaking
exercise: «Meet in person» means? | Meeting in a dream | *Meeting face to face, really there | Meeting by phone | Meeting on a screen
exercise: In grammar, which word is first person? | you | he or she | they | *I
test: «Each person has one life on this earth; nobody else can live it for them.» What does person mean here? | *One human being | A share of a price | A grammar word | Thing counted
test: A sign says «£5 per person». What does per person mean? | *For each person, a share | Many people together | For one special person only | A person's name
exam: In grammar, which words are third person? | we | *he or she | I | you
